      "textEn": "276\nThere is no such thing in the world that God is not connected to. We need that we find this\nrelationship of joining and connect with them through crime-free service. We can connect with them through their divine word utterance. The holy name of God and God himself are one, and whoever, with a sense of innocence, chants the holy name of God, immediately feels that God is present before him.\nEven through the vibrations of radio sound, we can attain a partial experience of sound,\nand by pronouncing the sound of divinity again, we can certainly experience the presence of God.\nIn this era, while every object is contaminated by the impurity of Kali, It is the order of the scriptures,\nand Lord Chaitanya Mahaprabhu has also given the same teaching that by chanting the holy name of God, we\ncan immediately be free from sin, and gradually Go back to the abode of the Lord, rising above the divine position\nCan be. A devotee who performs the innocent form of chanting the name of God is as auspicious as God himself.\nAnd by wandering in the world, all the sufferings of the world can be removed by devotees of God. Only\nBy propagating the chanting of the holy name of God, can we escape the evil effects of Kali Yuga.\nYo vai mamatibhramasurvansharajnya-\nMakshauhinishatamapanudadatmanatantra.\nTvam dushtamunpadamatmani paurushena\nSampadayant yadushu ramyambibhradangam. 34). Shabdartham\nYah- who; Vai- certainly; Mam- mine; Ati- extremely; Bharam-- extremely burdened; Asur- lineage; Rajnya- of kings;\nAkshauhini- one Akshauhini ( one Akshauhini has 21,870 chariots, just as many elephants, 109,350 infantry soldiers and 65,610\nmilitary horses ); Shatam- hundreds of such Akshauhinis; Apanudatt- destroyed; Atmanir- self-dependent; Tvam- to you;\nDushtam- putting in difficulty; Oon- foot; Apadam- without the power to stand; Atmani- inner; Paurushena- by the power of man;\nTo accomplish-- to complete; Yadushu-- in the Yadu dynasty; Ramyam-- divinely beautiful; Abhibharat-- accepted; Ankham-- body.\nOh, righteous man, I was burdened by the excessive military force employed by the atheistic kings,\nand now, by the grace of God, I have been able to overcome it. Similarly, you were also in a state of Huu\nand could not stand. In this way, to uplift you too, in the Yaduvansh, they\ndescended with their ST power."
